---
source: crates/engram-cli/tests/cli/snapshot/help.rs
expression: "f.run_bare(& [\"update\", \"--help\"])"
---
$ engramdb update --help
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Update an existing memory

Usage: engramdb update [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          Memory ID (supports prefix matching)

Options:
  -t, --type <TYPE>
          New type

  -c, --content <CONTENT>
          New content

  -s, --summary <SUMMARY>
          New summary

  -T, --title <TITLE>
          New title (short, a few words, for human-readable filenames)

  -p, --physical <PHYSICAL>
          New physical scope (replaces existing)

  -l, --logical <LOGICAL>
          New logical scope (replaces existing)

      --tags <TAGS>
          New tags (comma-separated or repeated, replaces existing)

      --tags-add <TAGS_ADD>
          Tags to add (comma-separated)

      --tags-remove <TAGS_REMOVE>
          Tags to remove (comma-separated)

      --criticality <CRITICALITY>
          New criticality

      --confidence <CONFIDENCE>
          New confidence

      --details <DETAILS>
          New details

      --details-file <DETAILS_FILE>
          Read details from file

      --visibility <VISIBILITY>
          New visibility

      --status <STATUS>
          New status

      --supersedes <SUPERSEDES>
          IDs of memories this one supersedes (comma-separated)

      --audience <AUDIENCE>
          Set the per-memory audience (project/group ids) for a group/global share (comma-separated). Only meaningful on a group/global memory

      --clear-audience
          Clear the audience (whole-group visibility). Wins over --audience

      --epistemic <EPISTEMIC>
          Epistemic class: fact, observation, or decision (defaults from type)

      --premise <PREMISE>
          Premise this memory depends on (e.g. "while we pin ort rc.12")

      --invalidated-by <INVALIDATED_BY>
          Paths/globs whose change invalidates this memory (repeatable)

      --origin-task <ORIGIN_TASK>
          Task/feature this memory was created for

      --generality <GENERALITY>
          Generality: project (default) or task

      --valid-from <VALID_FROM>
          Valid-time start (RFC3339) — backdate when the claim became true

      --clear-validity
          Clear the whole validity condition (premise/invalidated-by/origin-task/generality)

      --clear-invalidated
          Reopen a closed validity window (clears invalidated_at + superseded_by)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-friendly colored output with formatting
          - json:   JSON output for programmatic parsing
          - plain:  Plain text output without colors

      --invalidate
          Close the validity window now: the memory WAS true but no longer is. Preferred over delete — history stays queryable via --include-invalidated

      --json
          Output as JSON

      --superseded-by <SUPERSEDED_BY>
          Id of the memory that supersedes this one (only with --invalidate)

      --decay-strategy <DECAY_STRATEGY>
          Decay strategy: none, linear, exponential, or step

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

      --decay-half-life <DECAY_HALF_LIFE>
          Half-life in seconds for decay

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

      --decay-ttl <DECAY_TTL>
          TTL in seconds for decay

      --no-color
          No colored output

      --decay-floor <DECAY_FLOOR>
          Minimum decay factor (0.0-1.0)

      --dir <DIR>
          Working directory (default: current directory)

  -e, --editor
          Open memory file in $EDITOR

      --embedding-backend <EMBEDDING_BACKEND>
          Embedding backend: auto, onnx, or ollama

      --global
          Operate on the global (cross-project) memory store instead of the current project

      --in-process
          Force in-process model loading — never contact the shared embedding daemon. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_IN_PROCESS=1

      --group <GROUP>
          Update a memory in a named group store (instead of the current project)

      --spawn-daemon
          Spawn the shared embedding daemon if it is not already running, then route through it. By default the CLI only uses a daemon that is already running (connect-only)

      --no-maintenance
          Skip the automatic main-worktree maintenance pass (orphan-project cleanup + a quick store health check) for this invocation. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_DISABLE_AUTO_MAINTENANCE=1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr ---
